---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { APP_STORE_URL, SUPPORT_EMAIL, pathFor } from '../../config/site';
---
<SiteLayout title="Mobile app privacy policy" description="Golden Moments mobile app privacy policy: local picture activities, selected photos, backups, support communications, data choices, and contact information.">
  <section class="interior-hero">
    <div class="reading-column">
      <p class="eyebrow">Golden Moments / Legal</p>
      <h1>Mobile app privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="interior-lede">We want the app to be a comfortable place for family pictures and shared activities. This policy explains what stays on your device, what happens when you contact us, and where other services may be involved.</p>
      <p class="small-print">Effective October 18, 2026 · Applies to the Golden Moments mobile app</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="reading-column prose-page">
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p><strong>Cloudjet Solutions Pte. Ltd.</strong> (Singapore) publishes Golden Moments. This policy covers our mobile app for iPhone and iPad, including versions with optional locally stored family-photo activities. The current App Store release may differ from a feature being prepared for a future update. For the website, see our <a href={pathFor('/privacy/')}>separate website privacy notice</a>.</p>
    <p>Contact us about privacy by emailing <a href={'mailto:' + SUPPORT_EMAIL + '?subject=Golden%20Moments%20privacy'}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. Please do not include medical records, a diagnosis, or private family photographs in an initial request.</p>

    <h2>2. Information used on your device</h2>
    <p>Golden Moments can save game and sound preferences, information about available picture packs, and local files needed for its activities. This information helps the game work and remember settings. You do not need to register an account to play.</p>
    <p><strong>Selected family photos, when the feature is available in your installed version:</strong> You choose which pictures to import through the device's photo selection interface. The app creates smaller working copies in its own storage for matching and shared viewing. We do not operate a Golden Moments family-photo server or automatic sharing service, and the intended local-photo flow does not upload those working copies to us. We do not scan your entire library as part of that feature or change your original photographs.</p>
    <p>Pictures can contain information about people, including children. Consider their privacy and permission before selecting or showing pictures. The published App Store version may not yet include family-photo import.</p>
    <p>We do not ask users to enter diagnoses, medications, medical records, or cognitive test results. Playing a game is not a medical assessment. We do not intentionally derive an individual's dementia status or cognitive score from their moves.</p>

    <h2>3. When information can leave a device</h2>
    <p><strong>Device services and backups.</strong> Apple's photo picker, iCloud Photos, operating-system backups, App Store delivery, and optional device diagnostics are provided by Apple or other device services. If the picture you choose is stored only in iCloud, the operating system may need internet access to make it available. App data may be included in your device backup according to your settings. A copy stored in a device or cloud backup is not erased simply because you remove a copy from the app.</p>
    <p><strong>Earlier app versions and content services.</strong> Some older versions were designed to retrieve picture packs over the internet, while newer candidate builds include their starter library. When an app contacts a content host, normal technical connection information, such as an IP address and request details, can be visible to the service operator. We do not promise that every past or future version runs without network activity.</p>
    <p><strong>Third-party components.</strong> Development code for some versions includes Firebase-related software. In the current update candidate, analytics collection and automatic crash reporting are configured off; the distributed native binary and third-party manifests must still be checked before any updated App Store data-collection declaration is submitted. We do not represent the presence or absence of a code library as proof of actual data transmission. If a shipped version activates collection, we must first update the disclosures and, where required, obtain consent.</p>
    <p><strong>Contacting support.</strong> If you email us, we receive the email address, message, and any materials you choose to send. We use them to answer your question, handle privacy or rights requests, and meet applicable obligations. Your email provider and our email service provider necessarily handle the communication. Please do not send health information or family photos unless there is a clear need and you are comfortable doing so.</p>
    <p><strong>App Store activity.</strong> Apple operates app downloads, ratings, storefront transactions, and any App Store subscription or purchase functionality that may be offered in the future. We do not currently operate an in-app payment server. Apple's data-handling terms apply to information processed by Apple in those services.</p>

    <h2>4. Purposes, sharing, and safeguards</h2>
    <p>We use information under our control to provide the app's local features and respond to support, privacy, and rights requests. We do not sell selected family photographs or use them for targeted advertising. We do not offer social sharing or a photo-sync backend through this app.</p>
    <p>Where a service provider processes personal information for us, such as email support, we require appropriate confidentiality and security safeguards consistent with applicable legal duties. Independent services you choose to use, including Apple and GitHub, have their own privacy terms. We review third-party SDK use and data handling before new releases; we do not authorize new data-sharing purposes by merely linking to this policy.</p>
    <p>No system can guarantee absolute security. Protect your device with appropriate screen-lock and backup settings, and avoid showing or sending private family photographs without permission.</p>

    <h2>5. How long information is kept</h2>
    <p>Local game data and imported photo copies remain on the device until you remove them through available controls, delete the app and its data, or the operating system removes them. Removing one picture inside Golden Moments does not remove the original in Photos or copies held in existing backups. Offloading an app, rather than deleting it, may preserve its local data.</p>
    <p>Support emails and privacy requests are kept only as reasonably needed to respond, investigate issues, document compliance, resolve disputes, or meet applicable legal obligations. We review and delete information when it is no longer needed. We do not operate a remote account or photo collection to delete on your behalf.</p>

    <h2>6. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>You can choose not to import family photographs and can stop using the app without providing us with an account. If your installed version includes local photo import, use <strong>Your family photos → Remove</strong> or <strong>Remove all photo copies</strong> to delete working copies stored by the app; original photos are unaffected. To remove other app data, follow the operating system's <strong>Delete App</strong> process, not just <strong>Offload App</strong>. Check and manage device backups separately.</p>
    <p>You may ask about personal information that we hold (for example, a support conversation) or request access, correction, deletion, or other rights available under applicable law. Email <a href={'mailto:' + SUPPORT_EMAIL + '?subject=Golden%20Moments%20data%20request'}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>; we may ask for enough information to verify that we are responding to the right person. We will not request medical records as a condition of making a privacy request.</p>
    <p>Our <a href={pathFor('/privacy-choices/')}>privacy choices and deletion guide</a> provides practical steps. If personal information remains in an Apple backup or with an independently operated service, that provider's controls also apply.</p>

    <h2>7. Children and international services</h2>
    <p>Golden Moments is designed for older adults, families, and caregivers; it is not directed to children under 13. We do not ask children to open accounts or provide health information. If you believe a child sent us personal information through support, please contact us so we can address it appropriately.</p>
    <p>Cloudjet Solutions Pte. Ltd. is based in Singapore. Email support and third-party device/hosting services may process information in countries other than your own, subject to their applicable terms and legal requirements.</p>

    <h2>8. Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>We may update this notice when the app's features, third-party services, or legal obligations change. We will post a new effective date and provide additional notice or obtain consent when required by law. A new statement does not retroactively authorize previously undisclosed collection.</p>
    <p>Questions or privacy requests: <a href={'mailto:' + SUPPORT_EMAIL}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. For the app's intended use and limitations, see <a href={pathFor('/safety/')}>Safety and medical-use information</a>. For licensing, see <a href={pathFor('/terms/')}>Terms and app license information</a>.</p>
    <p class="back-home"><a class="text-link" href={pathFor('/legal/')}>← Legal information</a> · <a href={APP_STORE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">App Store listing</a></p>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
